{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ah, come in, sit. Your daughter can wait outside only, that is quite all right. How are you keeping, Mr. Rao?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ok is fine. What has brought you in today?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Hip checkup.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Yes. 6 weeks now since we replaced the right hip. Let me just think this through. You are walking in with a stick, I can see that.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Is the hip paining when you walk?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Good. And the calf, I was going to say the left, no, the right calf, the same side. Any swelling there? Any hardness?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. Let me see the wound itself. Stitches are gone, skin is dry, no redness, no ooze. I would say this wound has healed.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Good.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sister has left the observation slip. I will read it out loud so it is clear. Blood pressure today is one oh nine over seventy-seven millimetres of mercury.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Temperature thirty-seven point three, uh, sorry, wrong line. It is thirty-eight point three degrees celsius.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Pulse, she has put eighty-two, but that is the March column, err, I looked at the old row. Today the pulse is seventy-four per minute.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Right.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Weight today is sixty-one kilos. Last time in March you were sixty-eight. Your last pressure was one-forty, so today's reading is softer, which is all right.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): Thirty-eight point three is a little warm for 6 weeks, and the wound is so quiet. Are you feeling any chills, or feverish at home?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hmm. What all tablets then. You are still on the ecosprin?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right, that is the asprin, 75 milligrams, one tablet by mouth in the morning, for the clots.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): And the painkiller, the crocin. Paracetamol 500 milligrams by mouth. How many times a day?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Twice.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Twice is reasonable when the hip is not paining. Take it after food only.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): So, thinking it through, the wound has healed, there is no calf swelling, and you are up with the stick. The temperature is the only odd point. My working impression is ordinary recovery after the replacement, though I cannot rule out a small infection.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Hmm.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): I will book a blood test today, the CRP and the full count, so we see if the body is reacting.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): An ultrasound scan, we might do that if this warmth does not settle, not today. Let us see you in two weeks with the report. If the fever climbs or the calf swells, do not wait, come earlier. Keep the ecosprin going, and use the stick till I say otherwise.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok."
 ],
